WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.440
Once upon a time there was a small village deep in the mountains.

2
00:00:10.441 --> 00:00:16.166
To visitors, the village looked peaceful and beautiful.

3
00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:20.178
However the people in the village were very afraid.

4
00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:25.984
They were afraid of the tigers living in the mountains.

5
00:00:25.985 --> 00:00:30.312
The people in the village went into the mountains to hunt for food.

6
00:00:30.313 --> 00:00:32.893
But the tigers did not like that.

7
00:00:32.894 --> 00:00:37.280
The tigers frightened and chased the people out.

8
00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:39.976
The village decided to hold a meeting.

9
00:00:39.977 --> 00:00:43.600
They wanted to get rid of the tigers in the mountains.

10
00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:47.811
"We are tired of living in fear!" shouted one man.

11
00:00:47.812 --> 00:00:53.914
"What if the tigers come to our village and eat our children?" cried a woman.

12
00:00:53.915 --> 00:00:56.583
Finally a young man stood up.

13
00:00:56.584 --> 00:01:01.166
"We must make a trap to catch the tigers!" he said.

14
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:05.319
"What kind of trap?" asked another man.

15
00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.600
"We must dig very deep holes.

16
00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:13.848
The tigers will fall into them, but they will not be able to climb out," said the young man.

17
00:01:13.849 --> 00:01:18.937
Everyone cheered at the wonderful idea.

18
00:01:18.938 --> 00:01:22.799
The village worked day and night digging holes.

19
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.559
They dug holes around the village and up the road to the mountain.

20
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.845
At last they were done.

21
00:01:29.846 --> 00:01:33.206
One day a traveler was passing by the village.

22
00:01:33.207 --> 00:01:37.908
As he walked by a big hole in the ground, he heard a low roar.

23
00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:42.749
The traveler stopped and looked down the hole.

24
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.017
At the bottom of the hole was a tiger!

25
00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:52.546
"Oh please, kind sir, help me!" begged the tiger.

26
00:01:52.547 --> 00:02:00.814
"I promise never to forget your kindness if only you will help me!" cried the tiger.

27
00:02:00.815 --> 00:02:03.816
The traveler felt sorry for the tiger.

28
00:02:03.817 --> 00:02:07.921
He dragged a felled tree and lowered it into the hole.

29
00:02:07.922 --> 00:02:12.220
The tiger climbed out of the trap.

30
00:02:12.221 --> 00:02:16.203
"Thank you for your kindness," said the tiger.

31
00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:19.505
"And now, I am going to eat you."

32
00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:24.735
"But why? I just saved your life!" cried the traveler.

33
00:02:24.736 --> 00:02:33.397
"Because humans made those traps to catch tigers, and you are a human," said the tiger.

34
00:02:33.398 --> 00:02:36.853
The man was very frightened, but he had an idea.

35
00:02:36.854 --> 00:02:46.159
"It's not fair, Mr. Tiger, to judge one person the same as everyone else," the man said bravely.

36
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.075
"Let's hear what others have to say about this situation."

37
00:02:50.076 --> 00:02:54.663
The tiger agreed and the two of them set off.

38
00:02:54.664 --> 00:02:59.363
The man and the tiger went to an ox. They told him what happened.

39
00:02:59.364 --> 00:03:04.927
After listening the ox said, "Well, I have to agree with the tiger.

40
00:03:04.928 --> 00:03:06.916
Humans are cruel and mean.

41
00:03:06.917 --> 00:03:11.406
They tie us up and make us work hard all the time."

42
00:03:11.407 --> 00:03:17.188
Next they went to a pine tree. The pine tree listened to their story.

43
00:03:17.189 --> 00:03:23.498
Then it said, "Well, I have to agree with the tiger. Humans are unkind!

44
00:03:23.499 --> 00:03:28.783
They cut us down and throw us into the fire. Humans have no heart!"

45
00:03:28.784 --> 00:03:36.004
"You see? Humans are bad! Now, I'm going to eat you," the tiger said.

46
00:03:36.005 --> 00:03:41.637
The tiger was about to attack, when a rabbit came hopping by.

47
00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:44.680
"What's going on?" the rabbit asked.

48
00:03:44.681 --> 00:03:51.027
"Oh please, Mr. Rabbit," cried the traveler. "Listen and judge our case."

49
00:03:51.028 --> 00:03:57.850
"Fine, but we must hop back to where this all started," answered the rabbit.

50
00:03:57.851 --> 00:04:03.101
"Where were you before this human rescued you?" the rabbit asked the tiger.

51
00:04:03.102 --> 00:04:05.159
The tiger pointed to the trap.

52
00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:09.851
"I must see exactly where you were," said the rabbit.

53
00:04:09.852 --> 00:04:13.490
So the tiger jumped into the deep hole.

54
00:04:13.491 --> 00:04:19.298
"Was this felled tree in the hole when you fell into it, Mr. Tiger?" asked the rabbit.

55
00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:24.899
"No, no. There was nothing here," answered the tiger.

56
00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:29.015
So the traveler and the rabbit pulled the tree out.

57
00:04:29.016 --> 00:04:34.162
"You were trapped in this hole, with no one to help you.

58
00:04:34.163 --> 00:04:40.840
Then this kind man comes along and helps you, and now you want to kill him?

59
00:04:40.841 --> 00:04:44.892
That is not kind, Mr. Tiger," said the rabbit.

60
00:04:44.893 --> 00:04:50.205
"You complain that humans are unkind, but you are not being fair.

61
00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:57.116
You must not judge someone you have never met."

62
00:04:57.117 --> 00:05:00.681
The tiger remained ungrateful to the man who saved his life.

63
00:05:00.682 --> 00:05:06.878
So the traveler and the rabbit left the tiger in the hole and walked away.
